      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114355,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114356,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Botryoid odontogenic cyst (BOC)</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114357,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "<p >The cysts are mainly localized in the mandibular canine&nbsp;/ premolar alveolar bone, with 70% of LPCs and 85% of BOCs arising here; the remaining cases usually arise in the maxilla {26233969; 29156092}. Multifocal occurrence has been reported.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T16:51:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114358,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LPC and BOC are asymptomatic in almost 90% of cases and usually identified incidentally on radiographs. They cause buccal alveolar bone expansion in 50% of cases {29156092}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>LPC is a well-demarcated, often corticated unilocular radiolucency, closely related to the lateral surface of the root of an erupted tooth {6935584}. Cortical bone expansion and perforation may be evident on cone-beam imaging in half of all cases. Tooth roots are almost never resorbed. Most lesions are &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm in size. BOC has a multilocular appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114359,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LPCs and BOCs are rare, accounting for &lt;&nbsp;1% of odontogenic cysts {1501155; 30758760}. The majority present in the fifth to seventh decades of life {29156092} with a male preponderance {29156092}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114360,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114361,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LPC and BOC are developmental and thought to arise from odontogenic epithelial rests of dental lamina, reduced enamel epithelium, or rests of Malassez.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114362,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intact LPC presents as a small, tan, soft tissue cystic sac containing clear fluid. BOC is multilocular. The luminal surface of both may show focal thickenings {28153133}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114363,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p >LPC has an uninflamed fibrous wall lined by a thin, non-keratinized squamous or cuboidal epithelium 1&ndash;3&nbsp;cells thick. Focal, whorled, plaque-like epithelial thickenings are present, identical to those found less frequently in gingival cyst of the adult. Clear cells are often found in the thickenings {28153133}. BOC is multilocular with otherwise the same appearance {20952285}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T16:51:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114364,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 127,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:19:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
